    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1810.05184v1</id>
    <title>A virtually ample field that is not ample</title>
    <updated>2018-10-11T18:05:13Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.05184v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1810.05184v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>A field $K$ is called ample if for every geometrically integral $K$-variety $V$ with a smooth $K$-point, $V(K)$ is Zariski-dense in $V$. A field $K$ is virtually ample if some finite extension of $K$ is ample. We prove that there exists a virtually ample field that is not ample.</summary>
